VIOLATION — the artifact fails the rule-authoring meta-rules, and fails them on CONTENT rather
than on shape.

The substantive defect is that it adopts run-count minimisation as the criterion, which inverts
the parent contract. ci-cost-discipline.md bounds consolidation by revert-safety and states that
bundling unrelated work to hit a count is equally blocked; this artifact recommends exactly that
bundling on the ground that a combined run costs the same. It states that folding is cheaper
unconditionally and may be carried across from a sibling's measurement, where the parent makes the
mechanism conditional on two preconditions measured locally and records that it INVERTS where the
first is false. It licenses treating a queued cancelled run as costing nothing, which the parent's
MUST NOT forbids. And it licenses enabling a merge queue as a configuration improvement the agent
may apply, where the parent names that an operating-model change reserved to the owner.

AUTHORING DEFECTS COMPOUND IT. The section is headed for binding clauses while the modal
throughout is should / normally / usually / may, so nothing carries force. The DO/DO-NOT block
restates the heading in prose instead of showing two commands whose outcomes differ, so it teaches
nothing. The rationalization list is abstract paraphrase rather than matchable agent speech, so no
utterance can ever be recognised against it. The rationale asserts the belief under test — fewer
runs is cheaper — as its own justification.

NOT DEFECTS. The frontmatter, Wiring field set, Origin section and heading skeleton are well
formed and match the counterpart exactly; the pair is equalised on surface so neither size nor
section list can answer the question. The advisory severity follows from the inverted premise and
is not a separate finding.
